# Rust
/target/
**/target/
Cargo.lock

# Keep Cargo.lock for the CLI binary and examples (reproducible builds),
# but ignore it for library crates. Simplify for v1: ignore everywhere,
# revisit once ferrox-cli is a published binary.

# Build artifacts from ferrox's own pipeline
*.ferrox-out
ferrox-build/

# Keygen output (per-build generated, never committed)
**/keys.rs

# ferrox-mir-pass manual smoke-test scratch directory (Phase 7, step 7f-i):
# flatten_test.rs itself IS tracked (useful smoke-test source), but
# compiled artifacts from running ferrox-mir-driver.exe against it
# (flatten_test.exe, .pdb, and anything else generated there) are not.
scratch/*.exe
scratch/*.pdb
scratch/*.obj
scratch/*.pdb.lock

# Red-team harness scratch output
crates/ferrox-redteam/scratch/
*.ghidra_project/
*.gpr

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Env files
.env
.env.local
